          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em regular category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} finitely complete category
            which admits a good notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            factorization. A primary
            %em raison d’être
            behind regular categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is to have a decently behaved
            %em
              calculus of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relations"} relations
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rel"} Rel
          %p
            Regular categories also provide a natural
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semantics"} semantic
            environment to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interpretation"} interpret
            a particularly well behaved positive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fragment"} fragment
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+order+logic"} first order logic
            having connectives
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \top
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\wedge}
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∃
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+logic"} regular logic
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
          #RegularCategory.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (regular category)
              %br/
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is called
              %strong regular
              if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  it is
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} finitely complete
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi d
                                %msub
                                  %mo ×
                                  %mi c
                                %mi d
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi p
                                      %mn 1
                              %mtd
                                %mi d
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mrow
                                    %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                      %mrow
                                        %msub
                                          %mi p
                                          %mn 2
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mrow
                                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                      %mi f
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi d
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mi f
                              %mtd
                                %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        d\times_c d
                        \&amp;\stackrel{p_1}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                        d
                        \\\
                        {{}^\mathllap{p_2}}
                        \\big\downarrow
                        \&amp;&amp;
                        \\big\downarrow{{}^\mathrlap{f}}
                        \\\
                        d &amp;\stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; c
                        }
                %p
                  of any
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mi d
                        %mo →
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: d \to c
                  admits a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi c
                          %mi d
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo ⇉
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi d
                          %mo →
                          %mi coeq
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \times_c d \,\rightrightarrows\, d \to coeq(p_1,p_2)
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                  of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epimorphism
                  along any morphism is again a regular epimorphism.
            %p
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              The kernel pair is always a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence"} congruence
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              in
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi c
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ker(f) = d\times_c d
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ×
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \times d
              consisting of pairs of elements which have the same value under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              (sometimes called the “kernel” of a function in
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ker(f)
              as an internal
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              A map which is the coequalizer of a parallel pair of morphisms is called a
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epimorphism
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RegularCategory"}
              = succeed ".)" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Practical+Foundations"} Practical Foundations
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              The last condition in Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RegularCategory"}
              may equivalently be stated in the form “coequalizers of kernel pairs are
              = succeed "\u201D." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback-stable+colimit"} stable under pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi d
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \;\rightrightarrows\; d \to c
            %p
              along a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c' \to c
              is again a coequalizer diagram (nor need a regular category have coequalizers of all parallel pairs).
          %p
            In fact, a characterization equivalent to Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RegularCategory"}
            is:
          %p
          #CharacterizationViaImageFactorization.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              A
              %strong regular category
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} finitely complete category
              with a
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+factorization+system"} stable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+system"} factorizations
              in that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  every morphism factors as a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epimorphism
                  followed by a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              %li
                %p
                  these factorizations are preserved under
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %p
          (eg.
          = succeed "," do
            %a{:href => "#Gran20"} Gran 2020, Thm. 1.14
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/252842/381"} MO:a/252842
          %p
            See also
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/familial+regularity+and+exactness"} familial regularity and exactness
            for a generalization of this approach to include
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+category"} coherent
            categories as well.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p Examples of regular categories include the following:
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              is a regular category.
          %p
          #ToposesAreRegular.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              More generally, any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              is regular.
          (
          %a{:href => "#BarrGrilletvonOsdol"}> Barr, Grillet &amp; von Osdol 1971, p. 17
          ,
          = succeed "," do
            %a{:href => "#Borceux94III"} Borceux 1994III, Prop. 3.4.14
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#Johnstone02"} Johnstone 2002, p. 92
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Even more generally, a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+category"} locally cartesian closed category
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizers"} coequalizers
              is regular, and so any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasitopos"} quasitopos
              is regular.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+Lawvere+theory"} models
              of any finitary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+theory"} algebraic theory
              (i.e.,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is regular. This applies in particular to the category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
          %p
          #CategoryOfGroupsIsRegular.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
              of all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
              (including
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+groups"} non-abelian groups
          (e.g.
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#Borceux94II"} Borceux 1994 II, Ex. 2.4.3
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Actually, any category that is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functor"} monadic
              over
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              is regular. For example, the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frames"} frames
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Frm
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi Loc
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Frm \simeq Loc^{op}
              is regular, and the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} compact Hausdorff spaces
              is regular. A proof may be found
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits+in+categories+of+algebras#exact"} here
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
              is regular.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is regular, then so is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^D
              for any category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is regular and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod(T, C)
              of
              = succeed "-models" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is also regular. See Theorem 5.11 in Barr’s
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Barr"} Exact Categories
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice"} slice
              of a regular category is also regular; cf.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+regular+category"} locally regular category
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-slice"} co-slice
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borceux-Bourn"} Borceux-Bourn
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              is a quasitopos, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Q
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q^{op}
              is regular. Source: A2.6.3(i) in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Elephant
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ^{op}
              is regular. The key facts are that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+monomorphisms"} regular monomorphisms
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              are the same as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
              inclusions, and that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              of a subspace inclusion is a subspace inclusion as proven
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "subspace+topology#pushout"} there
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The category of (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"}> Hausdorff
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kelley+spaces"} Kelley spaces
              is regular (however, is not locally cartesian closed, nor is it
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+category"} exact
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#CagliariMatovaniVitale95"} Cagliari-Matovani-Vitale 95
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (counter-examples)
              Examples of categories which are
              %strong not regular
              include
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"}> Cat
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pos"} Pos
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %p The following example proves failure of regularity in all three cases:
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              be the poset
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{a, b\} \times (0 \to 1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              be the poset
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0 \to 1 \to 2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be the poset
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0 \to 2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p: A \to B
              obtained by identifying
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a, 1)
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (b, 0)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: C \to B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is the inclusion
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0, 2\} \to (0 \to 2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Pos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pos
              are not stable under pullback.
            %p
              Interpreting the posets as categories, the same example works for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+topological+spaces"} finite topological spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              of
              %em all
              topological spaces is not regular.
          %p However:
          %p
          #CompactlyGeneratedHausdorffSpacesAreRegular.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (compactly generated Hausdorff spaces form a regular category)
              %br/
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+category+of+topological+spaces"} convenient
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategories"} full subcategories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi kTop
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi kHaus
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    kTop
                    \\xhookrightarrow{\;}
                    kHaus
                    \\xhookrightarrow{\;}
                    Top
            %p
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+Hausdorff+spaces"} compactly generated Hausdorff spaces
              and of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+weakly+Hausdorff+spaces"} compactly generated weakly Hausdorff spaces
              are regular (
              %a{:href => "#CagliariMatovaniVitale95"}> Cagliari, Matovani &amp; Vitale 1995, p. 3
              ).
          %p
          #CompactlyGeneratedGSpacesFormARegularCategory.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (compactly generated
                = succeed "-spaces" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi Grp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi kTop
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \,\in\, Grp(kTop)
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+weakly+Hausdorff+space"} compactly generated weak Hausdorff
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+actions"} internal actions
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+G-spaces"} topological G-spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mi Act
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi kTop
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Act(kTop)
              is a regular category.
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mi Act
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi kTop
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi kTop
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Act(kTop) \xrightarrow{\;} kTop
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/created+limit"} creates
              all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              (
              %a{:href => "topological+G-space#ForgetfulFunctorCreatesLimitsAndColimits"}> this Prop.
              ). Since regularity is entirely a condition on limits and colimits (
              %a{:href => "regular+category#RegularCategory"}> this Def.
              ) the statement follows from Ex.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactlyGeneratedHausdorffSpacesAreRegular"}
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mal%27cev+theory"} Mal'cev theory
              (e.g., the theory of groups), then the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^T
              of
              = succeed "-models" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              is regular. This is because for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              Mal’cev, coequalizer maps in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^T
              are necessarily open surjections, and open surjections are stable under pullback.
