          %h2#references References
          %p The notion of regular categories was introduced in:
          %ul
            %li#BarrGrilletvonOsdol
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Barr"}> Michael Barr
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Grillet"} Pierre Grillet
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donovan+van+Osdol"} Donovan van Osdol
              = succeed "," do
                %em Exact Categories and Categories of Sheaves
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 236
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/BFb0058579"} doi:10.1007/BFb0058579
          %p Historical context:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              , Introduction of:
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topos+Theory"} Topos Theory
              (1977)
          %p Introduction:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carsten+Butz"}> Carsten Butz
                ,
                %em Regular Categories and Regular Logic
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRICS"} BRICS
                LS-98-2 Aarhus (1998) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.brics.dk/LS/98/2/"}> brics
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Gran20
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marino+Gran"}> Marino Gran
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An introduction to regular categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.08964"} arXiv:2004.08964
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.springerprofessional.de/en/new-perspectives-in-algebra-topology-and-categories/19764096"} ISBN:978-3-030-84319-9
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Freyd"}> Peter Freyd
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Scedrov"} Andre Scedrov
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories%2C+Allegories"} Categories, Allegories
                , North-Holland Amsterdam 1990. (chap. 1.5. pp.68ff)
            %li#Borceux94II
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                , Chapter 2 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categories and Structures
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 50
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511525865"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511525865
            %li#Borceux94III
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                , Section 3.3.4 of:
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categories of Sheaves
                %strong 50
                Cambridge University Press (1994) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511525872"}> doi:10.1017/CBO9780511525872
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Johnstone02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                , Section A1.3. pp.18ff of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant"} Sketches of an Elephant
                  I
                , Oxford UP 2002.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dominique+Bourn"}> Dominique Bourn
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marino+Gran"} Marino Gran
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Regular, Protomodular, and Abelian Categories
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walter+Tholen"} Walter Tholen
                (eds.),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categorical Foundations
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781107340985.007"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781107340985.007
          %p The following set of course notes has a section on regular categories
          %ul
            %li#vanOosten
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jaap+van+Oosten"}> Jaap van Oosten
              ,
              %em Basic category theory
              , BRICS LS-95-1 Aarhus 1995. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.staff.science.uu.nl/~ooste110/syllabi/catsmoeder.pdf#page=30"}> Section 4.1
              ) (
              %a{:href => "http://www.staff.science.uu.nl/~ooste110/syllabi/catsmoeder.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            An application of the regularity condition
            %sup#fnref:1
              %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
            is found in:
          %ul
            %li
              F. Knop,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Tensor envelopes of regular categories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0610552"} arXiv:math/0610552v2
          %p
            Generalization of the notion of regular categories to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brian+Day"}> Brian Day
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"} Ross Street
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Localisation of locally presentable categories
                %strong 58
                (1989) 227-233.
            %li
              %p
                Dimitri Chikhladze,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Barr’s embedding theorem for enriched categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 215
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0903.1173"} arxiv/0903.1173
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.jpaa.2010.12.004"} doi
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Lack"}> Stephen Lack
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giacomo+Tendas"} Giacomo Tendas
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Enriched regular theories
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 226
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.02301"} arXiv:1907.02301
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpaa.2019.106268"} doi
          %p
            Regularity of (Hausdorff)
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
          %ul
            %li#CagliariMatovaniVitale95
              F. Cagliari, S. Mantovani,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Enrico+Vitale"} Enrico Vitale
              = succeed "," do
                %em Regularity of the category of Kelley spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00872904"} doi:10.1007/BF00872904
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.dm.unibo.it/~cagliari/articoli/Regularkelley.pdf"} pdf
          .footnotes
            %hr/
            %ol
              %li#fn:1
                %p
                  Knop’s condition for regularity is slightly different from that presented here; he works with categories that when augmented by an absolutely initial object are regular in the terminology here. In the paper, Knop generalizes a construction of Deligne by showing how to construct a symmetric pseudo-abelian
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+category"} tensor category
                  out of a regular category through the calculus of relations.
                  %a{:href => "#fnref:1", :rev => "footnote"} ↩
